For those who haven't played Slash'Em, the poisonous cloak is a new
randomized appearance cloak appearing alongside the cloaks of
displacement, magic resistance, invisibility, and protection.
Basically, its addition means that trying on a random cloak can kill
you. ;)

Why do we need it? Trying on an unidentified cloak is already risky,
because a cursed cloak of invisibility bars a player from entering
shops or trying on body armor. The poison cloak is like an amulet of
strangulation, but amulets are much harder to identify and generally
less useful to an early player than cloaks are.

In my view, an item that can kill a careless player *but still be
useful in some situations* is true to the spirit of nethack. An iron
ball and chain bequeathed by a scroll of punishment can save a player
from sinking into lava. A ring of sustain ability protects from mind
flayer-induced brainlessness and aids in obtaining poison resistance
from poisonous corpses, even though it's a terrible ring to wear for
most anything else. And poisoned gloves could help an early player
without a better weapon option, sort of like a more powerful version
of kicking boots. They're sort of a more "useful" version of a
poisoned cloak.

Sure, since most players already can use poisoned weapons in some way,
and kicking boots already aid bare-handed combat, poisoned gloves
aren't a necessary addition. But I still think they'd be fun to use.



